Investigating matrix Schubert varieties -- basic functions for Schubert determinantal ideals
********************************************************************************************

Matrix Schubert varieties were introduced by Fulton [Ful92] in the study of
Schubert varieties in the complete flag variety. Their defining ideals are
called Schubert determinantal ideals.

  * [Ful92] William Fulton, Flags, Schubert polynomials, degeneracy loci, and
    determinantal formulas (see
    https://sites.math.washington.edu/~billey/classes/schubert.library/fulton.
    essential.set.pdf ), Duke Math J. 65 (1992): 381-420.
  * [HPW22] Zachary Hamaker, Oliver Pechenik, and Anna Weigandt, Gröbner
    geometry of Schubert polynomials through ice (see
    https://arxiv.org/abs/2003.13719 ), Advances in Mathematics 398 (2022):
    108228.
  * [KM05] Allen Knutson and Ezra Miller, Gröbner geometry of Schubert
    polynomials (see https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0110058 ), Annals of
    Mathematics (2005): 1245-1318.
  * [PSW24] Oliver Pechenik, David Speyer, and Anna Weigandt,
    Castelnuovo-Mumford regularity of matrix Schubert varieties (see
    https://arxiv.org/abs/2111.10681 ), Selecta Mathematica New Series 30, 66
    (2024).

The general method for creating a Schubert determinantal Ideal is *note
schubertDeterminantalIdeal: schubertDeterminantalIdeal,. The input is a
permutation in the form of a list. This package contains functions for
investigating the rank matrix (*note rankTable: rankTable,), the Rothe diagram
(*note rotheDiagram: rotheDiagram,), and the essential cells (*note
essentialSet: essentialSet,) of the Rothe diagram as defined by Fulton in
[Ful92].

