  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, 

Description
===========

Given an integer matrix (viewed as rank conditions to be imposed on a generic
matrix), returns the unique integer matrix that both defines the same ideal of
minors and also is the minimal rank table of some ASM.  See Section 1 and
Equation (21) of

  * [Wei]: Weigandt, Prism tableaux for alternating sign matrix varieties (see
    arXiv:1708.07236 (see https://arxiv.org/abs/1708.07236 )).



+-----------------------------------------------+
|i1 : M = matrix {{1,0,0},{0,23,24},{23,24,25}};|
|                                               |
|              3       3                        |
|o1 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ                         |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i2 : rankTableFromMatrix M                     |
|                                               |
|o2 = | 0 0 0 |                                 |
|     | 0 1 1 |                                 |
|     | 1 2 2 |                                 |
|                                               |
|              3       3                        |
|o2 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ                         |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i3 : N = matrix{{0,3,4},{1,1,1}};              |
|                                               |
|              2       3                        |
|o3 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ                         |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i4 : rankTableFromMatrix N                     |
|                                               |
|o4 = | 0 1 1 |                                 |
|     | 1 1 1 |                                 |
|                                               |
|              2       3                        |
|o4 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ                         |
+-----------------------------------------------+

