isPerm -- whether a list is a permutation in 1-line notation
************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        isPerm w
  * Inputs:
      * w, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, 

Description
===========

Given a list of length $n$, checks if the entries of the permutation are the
integers from 1 to $n$.

+-----------------------+
|i1 : w = {5,3,4,6,1,2} |
|                       |
|o1 = {5, 3, 4, 6, 1, 2}|
|                       |
|o1 : List              |
+-----------------------+
|i2 : isPerm w          |
|                       |
|o2 = true              |
+-----------------------+
|i3 : v = {4,3,2}       |
|                       |
|o3 = {4, 3, 2}         |
|                       |
|o3 : List              |
+-----------------------+
|i4 : isPerm v          |
|                       |
|o4 = false             |
+-----------------------+

Ways to use isPerm:
===================

  * "isPerm(List)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note isPerm: isPerm, is a *note method function:
(Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunction,.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

