composePerms -- computes the composition of two permutations
************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        composePerms(u,v)
  * Inputs:
      * u, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, 
      * v, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, 

Description
===========

Computes the composition of two permutations, $u$ and $v$, as $u*v$. Note that
the permutations must be written as a list in 1-line notation and must both be
permutations of (the same) $n$ letters.

+----------------------+
|i1 : u = {2,3,4,1}    |
|                      |
|o1 = {2, 3, 4, 1}     |
|                      |
|o1 : List             |
+----------------------+
|i2 : v = {4,3,2,1}    |
|                      |
|o2 = {4, 3, 2, 1}     |
|                      |
|o2 : List             |
+----------------------+
|i3 : composePerms(u,v)|
|                      |
|o3 = {1, 4, 3, 2}     |
|                      |
|o3 : List             |
+----------------------+
|i4 : u = {1,2,3,4,5}  |
|                      |
|o4 = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5}  |
|                      |
|o4 : List             |
+----------------------+
|i5 : v = {3,5,2,1,4}  |
|                      |
|o5 = {3, 5, 2, 1, 4}  |
|                      |
|o5 : List             |
+----------------------+
|i6 : composePerms(u,v)|
|                      |
|o6 = {3, 5, 2, 1, 4}  |
|                      |
|o6 : List             |
+----------------------+
|i7 : u = {3,5,2,1,4}  |
|                      |
|o7 = {3, 5, 2, 1, 4}  |
|                      |
|o7 : List             |
+----------------------+
|i8 : v = {1,2,3,4,5}  |
|                      |
|o8 = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5}  |
|                      |
|o8 : List             |
+----------------------+
|i9 : composePerms(u,v)|
|                      |
|o9 = {3, 5, 2, 1, 4}  |
|                      |
|o9 : List             |
+----------------------+

Ways to use composePerms:
=========================

  * "composePerms(List,List)"

For the programmer
==================

