isPatternAvoiding -- whether a permutation avoids certain patterns, e.g. $2143$-avoiding or $312$- and $231$-avoiding
*********************************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        isPatternAvoiding(w, pattern)
  * Inputs:
      * w, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, 
      * pattern, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, 

Description
===========

Given a permutation, checks if the permutation is pattern-avoiding, e.g.
$2143$-avoiding or $1432$-avoiding. For example, a permutation $w$ is
$2143$-avoiding if there does not exist indices $i < j < k < l$ such that $w_j
< w_i < w_l < w_k$.

+---------------------------------------+
|i1 : w = {7,2,5,8,1,3,6,4};            |
+---------------------------------------+
|i2 : pattern2143 = {2,1,4,3};          |
+---------------------------------------+
|i3 : isPatternAvoiding(w, pattern2143) |
|                                       |
|o3 = false                             |
+---------------------------------------+
|i4 : v = {2,3,7,1,5,8,4,6};            |
+---------------------------------------+
|i5 : pattern1432 = {1,4,3,2};          |
+---------------------------------------+
|i6 : isPatternAvoiding(v, pattern1432) |
|                                       |
|o6 = false                             |
+---------------------------------------+
|i7 : isPatternAvoiding({3,1,2},{3,1,2})|
|                                       |
|o7 = false                             |
+---------------------------------------+

Ways to use isPatternAvoiding:
==============================

  * "isPatternAvoiding(List,List)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note isPatternAvoiding: isPatternAvoiding, is a *note method
function: (Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunction,.

