isVexillary -- whether a permutation is vexillary, i.e. 2143-avoiding
*********************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        isVexillary w
  * Inputs:
      * w, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, 

Description
===========

Given a permutation in 1-line notation, checks if the permutation is vexillary,
i.e. $2143$-avoiding. A permutation $w$ is $2143$-avoiding if there do not
exist indices $i < j < k < l$ such that $w_j < w_i < w_l < w_k$.

+--------------------------------+
|i1 : w = {7,2,5,8,1,3,6,4}      |
|                                |
|o1 = {7, 2, 5, 8, 1, 3, 6, 4}   |
|                                |
|o1 : List                       |
+--------------------------------+
|i2 : isVexillary w              |
|                                |
|o2 = false                      |
+--------------------------------+
|i3 : v = {1,6,9,2,4,7,3,5,8}    |
|                                |
|o3 = {1, 6, 9, 2, 4, 7, 3, 5, 8}|
|                                |
|o3 : List                       |
+--------------------------------+
|i4 : isVexillary v              |
|                                |
|o4 = true                       |
+--------------------------------+

