isCDG -- whether a permutation is CDG
*************************************

  * Usage: 
        isCDG(perm)
  * Inputs:
      * perm, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, 

Description
===========

Given a permutation in 1-line notation, checks if the permutation is CDG.  We
say that a permutation $w$ is CDG if a certain modification (see [Kle23] for
precise description) of the Fulton generators of the Schubert determinantal
ideal $I_w$ form a diagonal Gröbner basis.  By [Kle23], $w$ is CDG if and only
if $w$ avoids all of the patterns $\{13254, 21543, 214635, 215364, 215634,
241635, 315264, 4261735\}$.

  * [Kle23] P. Klein, Diagonal degenerations of matrix Schubert varieties (see
    https://arxiv.org/abs/2008.01717 ), Algebr. Comb. 6 (2023), no. 4,
    1073-1094.



+--------------------------------+
|i1 : w = {7,2,5,8,1,3,6,4}      |
|                                |
|o1 = {7, 2, 5, 8, 1, 3, 6, 4}   |
|                                |
|o1 : List                       |
+--------------------------------+
|i2 : isCDG w                    |
|                                |
|o2 = true                       |
+--------------------------------+
|i3 : v = {1,6,9,2,4,7,3,5,8}    |
|                                |
|o3 = {1, 6, 9, 2, 4, 7, 3, 5, 8}|
|                                |
|o3 : List                       |
+--------------------------------+
|i4 : isCDG v                    |
|                                |
|o4 = true                       |
+--------------------------------+

Ways to use isCDG:
==================

  * "isCDG(List)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note isCDG: isCDG, is a *note method function:
(Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunction,.

