PipeDream -- the class representing a pipe dream
************************************************

Description
===========

A pipe dream is stored as a square array containing "+" and "/" symbols. The
"+" symbols are interpreted as crossing tiles and the "/" are interpreted as
bump tiles. Starting on the left edge, the path starting at row $i$ will end at
column $w_i$.

+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : L = {{"+", "/", "/"}, {"+", "/", "/"}, {"/", "/", "/"}}|
|                                                            |
|o1 = {{+, /, /}, {+, /, /}, {/, /, /}}                      |
|                                                            |
|o1 : List                                                   |
+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : D = PipeDream L                                        |
|                                                            |
|o2 = +//                                                    |
|     +//                                                    |
|     ///                                                    |
|                                                            |
|o2 : PipeDream                                              |
+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : L == toList D                                          |
|                                                            |
|o3 = true                                                   |
+------------------------------------------------------------+
* Menu:

* pipeDreams::                  computes the set of reduced pipe dreams corresponding to a permutation
* pipeDreamsNonReduced::        computes the set of all pipe dreams corresponding to a permutation

